CHAPTER.VERS:
[There shall be] no more praise of Moab: in Heshbon they have devised evil against it;
Thus shall the Babylonians encourage one another. come, and let us cut it off from [being] a nation. Also thou shalt be cut down,
Read (Isa_25:10). O Madmen; the sword shall pursue thee.

I know his wrath, saith the LORD; 

          He will not execute his malice against his neighbours.
         but [it shall] not [be] so; his lies shall not so effect [it].

From the cry of Heshbon [even] to Elealeh, [and even] to Jahaz, have they uttered their voice, from Zoar [even] to Horonaim, [as] an 

          {{See Isa_15:5}}
         heifer of three years old: for the waters also of Nimrim shall be desolate.
